---
source: crates/yokectl/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: stdout
---
Install a profile from a local file path, an HTTP(S) URL, or a bare community-index name. The source is auto-classified: an existing local file becomes a path source; a parseable http(s) URL becomes a URL source (Google Sheets URLs are rewritten to their CSV-export form); anything else is resolved through the community index. Parse and validate gate the write by default; --no-validate is an escape hatch.

Usage: yokectl install [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>

Arguments:
  <SOURCE>
          Local path, URL, or community-index name

Options:
      --as <AS_NAME>
          Destination filename on the volume (overrides default)

      --fake-volume <FAKE_VOLUME>
          Use a directory as a fake volume backend instead of the platform device

      --dry-run
          Print the destination without writing

      --json
          Emit machine-readable JSON on stdout (NDJSON for watch)

      --no-validate
          Skip parse and validate (escape hatch; warns on stderr)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase tracing verbosity on stderr; repeat (-vv reveals info, -vvv debug)

      --no-color
          Disable ANSI styling (NO_COLOR=1 or non-TTY stdout also disable)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
